WEBVTT

01:10.290 --> 01:12.840
Hey, this is great! All these posters!

01:13.340 --> 01:16.930
And they're playing
the opening theme song over there!

01:16.930 --> 01:18.550
Hey, Eita,

01:18.550 --> 01:20.390
the menu's pretty cool too.

01:20.680 --> 01:23.640
They're all named
after the dungeon bosses.

01:23.640 --> 01:25.640
Some are real blasts from the past!

01:25.640 --> 01:28.520
Hey! Talk about eagle eyes, Mr. Kamota!

01:28.520 --> 01:29.690
Let me see! Let me see!

01:30.440 --> 01:31.980
And they actually look good!

01:31.980 --> 01:33.570
What's everyone having?

01:33.570 --> 01:34.530
<i>Uh-oh.</i>

01:34.900 --> 01:37.780
<i>I know Yamada and Rurihime,</i>

01:37.780 --> 01:40.200
Scorching Hot Salamander Curry!
<i>but who is this old guy
and the one wearing glasses?</i>

01:40.200 --> 01:40.700
Scorching Hot Salamander Curry!

01:40.700 --> 01:41.830
That brings back memories!

01:42.200 --> 01:44.700
Are you into spicy foods, Eita?

01:44.700 --> 01:47.370
Actually, I love sweets!

01:48.580 --> 01:50.290
<i>They look like they're having a blast.</i>

01:51.210 --> 01:52.500
Rurihime...

01:53.210 --> 01:56.340
who are those two?
They're in our guild, right?

01:57.680 --> 01:59.480
That's Mr. Kamota and Eita.

01:59.480 --> 02:00.090
Huh?

02:00.090 --> 02:03.430
Uh, right. Can you tell me
a little more about them?

02:05.470 --> 02:08.730
By the way,
my character name isn't Rurihime.

02:10.650 --> 02:14.320
And I'm actually wondering
who you are.

03:45.780 --> 03:46.990
Huh?

03:48.160 --> 03:50.750
Um, what do you mean?

03:52.160 --> 03:55.710
What is this? Why are you
sitting in on our guild's meetup?

03:56.880 --> 04:00.030
What? You're Rurihime, right?

04:00.030 --> 04:01.550
I told you I'm not.

04:01.550 --> 04:02.380
But...

04:02.720 --> 04:05.760
Never mind me. Who are you?

04:06.680 --> 04:08.430
Hold on a second.

04:08.430 --> 04:10.560
Then where's Rurihime?

04:10.560 --> 04:12.810
- Rurihime...
- I just said—

04:12.810 --> 04:17.770
Eita, shouldn't we introduce ourselves
before we order?

04:19.530 --> 04:21.190
You have a point there!

04:21.190 --> 04:22.780
Sorry about that, Akanecchi!

04:23.650 --> 04:25.030
Once again...

04:26.160 --> 04:28.080
Eita Sakaki, age 19.

04:28.080 --> 04:29.660
Hobby: online gaming.

04:29.660 --> 04:32.040
I'm the one who plays Rurihime!

04:32.580 --> 04:33.460
Nice to meet you.

04:33.960 --> 04:36.130
Akanecchi!

04:39.210 --> 04:40.050
Ne...

04:40.300 --> 04:41.710
"Nekama" means...

04:42.260 --> 04:44.680
a guy posing as a woman online,

04:44.680 --> 04:48.970
where his true appearance
and identity remain unknown,

04:48.970 --> 04:51.930
the actual person posing as a woman,
or the act of doing so.

04:51.930 --> 04:54.140
It's an abbreviation
of the term "net okama,"

04:54.140 --> 04:55.560
which has been in use

04:55.560 --> 04:58.230
since the pre-Internet days
of online communications.

04:58.650 --> 04:59.900
Ne...ka...

04:59.900 --> 05:01.230
You couldn't be more wrong!

05:02.230 --> 05:06.610
I am a gear that moves my muse,
who descended upon the cyberspace sea.

05:06.610 --> 05:09.160
In other words, Rurihime and I
are one and the same

05:09.160 --> 05:10.780
and yet totally different!

05:11.160 --> 05:15.000
I'm loathe to describe this unique state
with a cheap term like "Nekama,"

05:15.000 --> 05:17.920
or should I say
it's not as simple as that?

05:17.920 --> 05:19.460
I mean, in the 2D world,

05:19.460 --> 05:22.000
Rurihime and I are, if anything,
bound by a common destiny.

05:22.000 --> 05:25.930
Like, she's my goddess, my mother,
my bride, and my alter ego?

05:26.220 --> 05:28.090
When a guy starts using
a female character,

05:28.090 --> 05:30.760
they cry "Nekama! Nekama!"
but what do they know?

05:30.760 --> 05:32.350
In that regard, Rurihime and I have
a more creative kind of relationship, see?

05:32.350 --> 05:33.520
Eita...
In that regard, Rurihime and I have
a more creative kind of relationship, see?

05:33.520 --> 05:34.600
In that regard, Rurihime and I have
a more creative kind of relationship, see?

05:34.600 --> 05:36.890
Not that this is easy
for most people to understand,

05:36.890 --> 05:37.230
but what I'm trying to say is—

05:37.230 --> 05:38.310
Eita...
but what I'm trying to say is—

05:39.440 --> 05:41.770
Not everyone's as enthusiastic as you.

05:42.650 --> 05:44.320
Hey, I gave you my number

05:44.320 --> 05:46.400
and turned to you
for advice about being dumped!

05:46.400 --> 05:49.490
Calm down, Akanecchi. It's all good.

05:49.490 --> 05:51.490
Because that wasn't me. It was Rurihime.

05:51.490 --> 05:53.040
What does that even mean?

05:53.040 --> 05:54.250
Um...

05:54.370 --> 05:56.580
I'm Takezo Kamota.

05:56.580 --> 06:00.630
My character name is takezo,
spelled out in English.

06:00.630 --> 06:05.840
I'm usually grinding in the dungeons,
so we've never met as characters.

06:05.840 --> 06:08.220
And this young girl is Runa.

06:08.930 --> 06:13.510
She's Eita's younger sister
and the model for Rurihime.

06:14.430 --> 06:17.480
How creepy is it to base your character
on your own kid sister?

06:19.350 --> 06:22.480
And that's Akito Yamada.

06:22.480 --> 06:25.900
Wait, you two already
know each other, right?

06:25.900 --> 06:28.950
Huh? What does that mean?
You know each other?

06:29.160 --> 06:32.450
What are you two?
How do you know each other, exactly?

06:32.450 --> 06:35.790
Huh? Uh, actually...

06:37.790 --> 06:39.960
It's too complicated to explain.

06:39.960 --> 06:41.040
It's a long story, so—

06:41.040 --> 06:44.040
No, it's not!
We met at an event, that's all!

06:44.960 --> 06:46.800
In a nutshell, yeah.

06:48.300 --> 06:51.340
Well, it's not like
I wasn't starting to realize...

06:56.810 --> 06:58.980
<i>I knew it, she totally hates me!</i>

07:01.310 --> 07:02.980
<i>Oh, but...</i>

07:04.360 --> 07:05.190
I see.

07:06.320 --> 07:10.030
It was you and Eita
that I saw in the game.

07:11.070 --> 07:14.580
I mean, you were kind of flirting,
so I thought you were a couple!

07:15.120 --> 07:17.080
He was an upperclassman back home,

07:17.080 --> 07:20.830
so when he's totally in character,
I've got to play along.

07:20.830 --> 07:22.920
Yamada!

07:23.630 --> 07:25.380
Flirt, flirt! Flirt, flirt!

07:25.380 --> 07:26.380
Upperclassman's orders.

07:26.380 --> 07:28.460
I see. That must be tough.

07:33.430 --> 07:36.970
You told me before that you
didn't have a girlfriend...

07:37.680 --> 07:39.100
so I thought it was a lie.

07:40.850 --> 07:43.350
I wouldn't lie about something like that.

07:44.440 --> 07:46.360
Right! Of course you wouldn't.

07:46.360 --> 07:47.190
I'm so glad!

07:50.530 --> 07:51.360
<i>Wait...</i>

07:53.820 --> 07:56.700
<i>What did I just say?</i>

07:58.410 --> 07:59.660
You're so glad?

08:02.330 --> 08:03.830
"I'm so glad"?

08:03.830 --> 08:05.040
Is that what you just said?

08:06.500 --> 08:10.340
Just what did you mean by "glad"?

08:13.380 --> 08:15.140
Akane, could it be...

08:16.760 --> 08:19.520
are you in love with Yamada?

08:21.980 --> 08:23.020
N-No...

08:23.940 --> 08:25.650
Sorry, Akanecchi!

08:25.650 --> 08:27.770
Not only is my sister
super territorial,

08:27.770 --> 08:29.690
she's in the throes
of adolescent rebellion,

08:29.690 --> 08:31.150
so she can be really abrasive!

08:31.690 --> 08:33.320
Really, now! We can't have that, Runa.

08:33.320 --> 08:35.320
That's so rude,
talking to an older girl like that—

08:35.320 --> 08:37.410
Oh, no, it's totally fine, all right?

08:37.580 --> 08:40.290
If you act like that, you're going
to have a hard time in life!

08:40.290 --> 08:41.620
Back off, Nekama.

08:41.830 --> 08:43.750
I'm not a Nekama! I'm a romanticist!

08:43.750 --> 08:44.750
Shut up.

08:44.750 --> 08:46.130
Please don't fight.

08:46.380 --> 08:50.130
Uh, does everyone know what they want?

08:50.130 --> 08:52.130
What should I order?

08:53.260 --> 08:54.800
<i>What a shock.</i>

09:11.730 --> 09:13.190
Should we get someone to take our—

09:14.490 --> 09:15.990
Oh!

09:16.280 --> 09:18.240
Are you okay, Akane?

09:18.240 --> 09:20.240
I-I'm so sorry! It slipped out of my hand!

09:21.160 --> 09:23.370
Are you hurt? Let's call someone over!

09:23.370 --> 09:25.080
It's fine! I can do it.

09:30.750 --> 09:33.550
You could hurt yourself,
so we should let the staff handle it.

09:38.430 --> 09:40.470
I-I guess you're right.

09:43.060 --> 09:46.270
Excuse me! We broke a glass over here!

09:48.270 --> 09:52.820
<i>This is crazy.
I mean, I didn't see that coming.</i>

09:54.190 --> 09:55.240
<i>What am I going to do?</i>

09:55.740 --> 09:57.700
<i>I just know my face's red!</i>

09:58.280 --> 10:01.870
<i>Should I run to the restroom?
Would that be unnatural?</i>

10:02.700 --> 10:05.450
<i>But I've got to pull myself together fast.</i>

10:05.830 --> 10:09.120
Uh, excuse me.
I'm going to go make a call.

10:09.120 --> 10:09.960
Sure.

10:09.960 --> 10:13.300
Oh, what are you having?
I'll order for you.

10:13.300 --> 10:14.800
Please go ahead and order first.

10:21.930 --> 10:23.470
<i>Thank goodness.</i>

10:23.470 --> 10:24.680
Are you all right?

10:24.680 --> 10:26.100
Oh, yes.

10:27.600 --> 10:30.270
Sorry! I think I feel the call of nature.

10:30.270 --> 10:32.060
<i>So he's Rurihime, huh?</i>

10:33.020 --> 10:34.360
<i>She's still staring at me!</i>

10:35.900 --> 10:37.360
Enjoy!

10:37.950 --> 10:39.240
Thank you very much.

10:39.740 --> 10:40.990
Feel better now?

10:40.990 --> 10:43.030
Yes! Sorry to cause a commotion.

10:43.530 --> 10:45.950
So glad that you didn't hurt yourself.

10:45.950 --> 10:47.120
Thank you so much!

10:47.410 --> 10:49.870
<i>Mr. Kamota's so nice!</i>

10:50.170 --> 10:55.630
Since this is your first offline meetup,
Akane, we were all looking forward to it.

10:55.630 --> 10:57.880
No one told me about it,
and I'm not having fun.

10:59.010 --> 11:01.720
Have you all known each other long?

11:01.720 --> 11:05.350
The four of us met in a previous game.

11:05.350 --> 11:08.350
We started playing FOS
when Eita asked us to.

11:08.850 --> 11:12.650
Runa here hardly ever logs in, though.
We see her maybe once every three months?

11:12.650 --> 11:13.480
<i>I see.</i>
Runa here hardly ever logs in, though.
We see her maybe once every three months?

11:13.480 --> 11:14.060
MMO is a drag.

11:14.060 --> 11:15.020
<i>So aside from me, everyone
at this meetup knows each other.</i>
MMO is a drag.

11:15.020 --> 11:16.690
<i>So aside from me, everyone
at this meetup knows each other.</i>

11:16.980 --> 11:18.860
Eita was so excited about today,

11:18.860 --> 11:23.120
saying there was a lovely person that he
couldn't wait to welcome into our guild.

11:23.450 --> 11:25.660
Hey! You're not going after
my brother too, are you?

11:25.660 --> 11:26.620
No, I am not!

11:32.210 --> 11:34.250
I thought you never lied.

11:35.500 --> 11:37.130
But you lied about making a call.

11:41.300 --> 11:42.130
What happened?

11:43.300 --> 11:44.350
Somehow...

11:45.680 --> 11:48.640
I got the feeling that I
should vanish from her sight.

11:48.640 --> 11:50.390
<i>You stay away from me.</i>

11:50.680 --> 11:52.390
She was giving off that kind of aura.

11:53.230 --> 11:55.360
So that's how you interpreted it.

11:56.020 --> 12:00.070
I think what Runa said to her
really upset her.

12:00.070 --> 12:03.070
If you ask me, I think Akanecchi
was just a little embarrassed.

12:03.740 --> 12:04.990
Why would she be embarrassed?

12:04.990 --> 12:06.160
Don't make me say it.

12:06.660 --> 12:08.740
But I won't know what it is
unless you say it.

12:09.750 --> 12:11.660
Well, that's the kind of guy you are.

12:12.160 --> 12:13.420
Not that I mind.

12:13.830 --> 12:17.550
Still, real-life Akanecchi
sure is pretty, huh?

12:17.550 --> 12:21.550
You said she was just like her character,
so I thought she'd be more childish.

12:23.300 --> 12:25.300
<i>Yamada!</i>

12:25.300 --> 12:26.510
<i>- Yamada!
- Yamada!</i>

12:27.600 --> 12:28.970
She's totally like that, though.

12:28.970 --> 12:29.810
Huh?

12:30.100 --> 12:32.600
Come on,
she's nothing like that character!

12:32.600 --> 12:33.690
You think?

12:33.690 --> 12:37.020
I mean, the female characters in FOS
are all the little-girl type, anyway.

12:37.860 --> 12:40.730
Well, it's not like I can tell
the difference between girls.

12:40.730 --> 12:44.910
You're never going to find yourself
a girlfriend with that kind of attitude.

12:47.660 --> 12:51.000
Isn't giving me a hard time
about not having a girlfriend getting old?

12:51.580 --> 12:55.580
It used to be fun, but these days,
I'm starting to worry.

12:57.380 --> 13:00.250
Your indifference towards girls
is abnormal.

13:04.630 --> 13:05.550
Yeah.

13:13.480 --> 13:15.520
<i>Did you feel sorry for me?</i>

13:31.870 --> 13:32.910
<i>Did you?</i>

13:42.380 --> 13:43.670
<i>Goodbye.</i>

13:52.930 --> 13:54.730
Thank you very much!

13:55.060 --> 13:57.230
All right, that's it for now!

13:57.230 --> 14:01.520
There's a guild battle tonight,
so let's meet up again online!

14:01.520 --> 14:02.980
- Okay!
- Okay!

14:03.280 --> 14:05.990
Sorry I can't walk you home, Akanecchi!

14:06.280 --> 14:08.240
If only I didn't have to head to work now.

14:08.240 --> 14:10.990
And you got lost earlier.
That worries Ruri!

14:10.990 --> 14:12.240
I'll be fine.

14:14.200 --> 14:16.080
What's wrong, Runa?

14:16.080 --> 14:17.500
Glaring like that...

14:18.460 --> 14:20.210
Runa doesn't like her.

14:20.710 --> 14:23.420
Clinging onto Yamada and my brother...

14:24.460 --> 14:26.010
she's like a bitch.

14:26.010 --> 14:26.840
Bi—

14:26.840 --> 14:29.510
Oh, dear!
Where'd you hear such a word, Runa?

14:30.090 --> 14:32.560
<i>It's always been
the four of us playing together.</i>

14:32.560 --> 14:34.970
<i>Why should we let that girl in now?</i>

14:36.520 --> 14:40.980
<i>I'm going to kick her out of our guild
if it's the last thing I do.</i>

14:47.070 --> 14:47.950
Hmm.

14:48.820 --> 14:51.870
<i>Hey! We're headed in the same direction,
so let's go home together!</i>

14:52.450 --> 14:57.660
<i>So I blurted that out impulsively,
but the conversation's not taking off.</i>

14:58.500 --> 14:59.580
Hey, Yamada.

15:00.040 --> 15:00.960
Yes?

15:01.500 --> 15:04.000
Do you guys hang out together
like this sometimes?

15:04.000 --> 15:04.840
Yes.

15:04.840 --> 15:07.010
Really? So you all get along, huh?

15:07.590 --> 15:08.470
I guess so.

15:08.630 --> 15:11.260
Oh, hey! Eita sure is a fun guy, huh?

15:11.760 --> 15:12.600
Yes.

15:14.390 --> 15:15.970
<i>Um...</i>

15:27.190 --> 15:28.490
Huh? Huh?

15:30.740 --> 15:31.700
Whoa.

15:32.740 --> 15:34.070
Ouch.

15:34.070 --> 15:35.080
Are you all right?

15:35.080 --> 15:35.990
Sorry.

15:36.830 --> 15:38.290
You should switch places with me.

15:38.700 --> 15:40.460
What? It's all right. I couldn't do that.

15:40.460 --> 15:41.330
It's fine.

15:41.830 --> 15:42.750
Thanks.

15:43.250 --> 15:44.080
Huh?

15:47.380 --> 15:48.210
Oh.

15:49.130 --> 15:51.050
<i>Ah, it's him.</i>

15:51.590 --> 15:55.390
Whoa. For a second, I thought
they were staring at me.

15:57.390 --> 16:00.850
<i>Well, I was taken aback
by his good looks at first too.</i>

16:01.850 --> 16:04.360
<i>...are you in love with Yamada?</i>

16:06.900 --> 16:09.530
<i>Is that what it looked like to her?</i>

16:10.030 --> 16:11.280
<i>Not good! Not good!</i>

16:11.280 --> 16:13.360
<i>Yamada's a valued online gamer friend!</i>

16:13.820 --> 16:16.240
Oh, hey, Yamada,
what are you having for dinner?

16:16.660 --> 16:18.580
Well, I'm not that hungry.

16:18.580 --> 16:19.410
You're not?

16:19.910 --> 16:20.830
Pudding or something.

16:21.660 --> 16:23.000
What, are you serious?

16:24.830 --> 16:27.130
That will be 128 yen.

16:28.300 --> 16:29.920
Thank you very much!

16:29.920 --> 16:33.000
Um, so you were
being serious just now?

16:33.000 --> 16:33.630
Yes.

16:35.800 --> 16:38.390
- Do you live alone, Yamada?
- Yes.

16:38.390 --> 16:39.810
And you don't cook at home?

16:39.810 --> 16:40.640
Not at all.

16:41.140 --> 16:44.480
What? Then what do you eat every day?

16:44.980 --> 16:47.400
I buy food from convenience stores
and stuff.

16:48.020 --> 16:49.280
Oh, really?

16:49.780 --> 16:52.650
<i>Yamada's a high school student, right?</i>

16:54.150 --> 16:56.620
<i>Doesn't his mom say anything about that?</i>

16:57.830 --> 17:01.040
<i>But I shouldn't really pry
into someone's family life.</i>

17:02.620 --> 17:03.620
Hmm.

17:04.370 --> 17:05.420
Hey! Yamada!

17:05.420 --> 17:06.830
Do you have a little time now?

17:06.830 --> 17:07.670
Yes.

17:07.840 --> 17:10.840
Fifteen... no, ten minutes!
Wait here for ten minutes, will you?

17:10.840 --> 17:11.920
I'll be right back!

17:27.190 --> 17:28.150
<i>Ten minutes.</i>

17:30.360 --> 17:32.110
<i>But she seemed so down...</i>

17:34.740 --> 17:36.610
Yamada! Long time no see!

17:40.030 --> 17:41.910
<i>People do bounce back, then, I guess.</i>

18:07.270 --> 18:08.900
Yamada!

18:11.520 --> 18:14.360
Th-Thanks for waiting!

18:14.610 --> 18:15.440
Huh?

18:20.700 --> 18:22.330
Hey, are you okay?

18:22.330 --> 18:26.120
Oh, man. I haven't run like my life
depended on it... since high school.

18:27.750 --> 18:30.380
What's in these big bags?

18:30.710 --> 18:33.000
Oh, this here's curry!

18:34.300 --> 18:36.510
I'm pretty sure
you don't cook rice at home,

18:36.510 --> 18:38.680
so I brought some frozen rice too.

18:39.090 --> 18:43.350
I just made this curry this morning,
so it'll be good for at least two days.

18:43.850 --> 18:47.560
Since I'm strapped for cash this month,
there's not much meat in it.

18:47.690 --> 18:48.810
But to make up for that...

18:49.310 --> 18:51.190
I'm giving you the salad
and pickled veggies

18:51.190 --> 18:52.860
I just bought at the convenience store!

18:52.860 --> 18:54.320
No. Uh...

18:54.530 --> 18:56.570
I wouldn't feel right about that,
so it's okay.

18:56.570 --> 18:58.070
You did just say money's tight too.

18:58.070 --> 19:00.610
You have to eat right,
or you won't grow up!

19:00.610 --> 19:01.450
Well, but...

19:02.370 --> 19:03.660
Pudding is for dessert!

19:04.160 --> 19:05.830
Well, yeah, but...

19:06.410 --> 19:08.410
From one guildmate to another!

19:09.500 --> 19:10.420
But...

19:13.040 --> 19:14.750
That's your phone ringing.

19:15.250 --> 19:16.590
Oh, it's mine?

19:17.050 --> 19:19.380
Wonder who it is? Momo, maybe?

19:22.180 --> 19:24.760
Huh? I don't know this number.

19:26.020 --> 19:27.430
Yes? Hello?

19:29.600 --> 19:32.020
Oh, um...

19:33.360 --> 19:34.230
<i>This is Runa.</i>

19:36.190 --> 19:39.280
Runa? Hey, what's up?

19:39.610 --> 19:43.950
<i>I got your number from my brother.
Sorry I didn't ask you.</i>

19:43.950 --> 19:45.030
That's okay!

19:45.700 --> 19:50.160
<i>I'm sorry for being so rude to you
when you came just to meet us.</i>

19:51.250 --> 19:53.540
My brother told me to apologize too.

19:53.750 --> 19:56.460
What? I don't mind at all!

19:56.460 --> 19:59.300
Who doesn't get nervous meeting
people for the first time?

20:00.050 --> 20:04.970
So if you want,
I'd like to hang out again.

20:06.390 --> 20:10.350
<i>Next time, I want to do it right
and get closer to you.</i>

20:10.890 --> 20:12.100
Runa...

20:14.900 --> 20:15.940
Okay!

20:16.730 --> 20:17.570
Sure.

20:18.400 --> 20:21.490
Next Saturday, right?
Yes, sounds good!

20:21.990 --> 20:24.820
Sure! I'm looking forward to it too!

20:25.660 --> 20:26.490
Bye!

20:27.580 --> 20:29.790
I'm going to hang out with Runa!

20:29.790 --> 20:31.750
Uh, right. I could hear.

20:32.710 --> 20:36.000
I thought she couldn't stand me,
so this makes me happy.

20:36.920 --> 20:40.050
I wonder what Runa's like in-game?

20:40.050 --> 20:41.090
Do you know, Yamada?

20:41.090 --> 20:41.920
A little.

20:41.920 --> 20:43.970
What's her Job Class,
and what does she use?

20:43.970 --> 20:45.510
Is she a Wizard, maybe?

20:45.510 --> 20:47.050
I'd love to see her sometime!

20:47.050 --> 20:49.390
What level is she, I wonder?

20:51.180 --> 20:52.310
That's great.

20:52.310 --> 20:55.520
Yeah! I'm going to add
Runa's number to my contacts!

21:07.490 --> 21:09.290
<i>She said Saturday, right?</i>

21:12.790 --> 21:15.620
<i>Runa Sasaki, tutoring job.</i>

21:17.290 --> 21:18.340
<i>That's what I thought.</i>

21:23.170 --> 21:24.680
<i>Maybe I heard her wrong.</i>

22:57.060 --> 23:00.940
Today, I'm going to show you
the avatars Rurihime likes to use!

23:03.690 --> 23:07.070
First, Alice's Flower Clock Set!

23:07.070 --> 23:09.200
It's a really popular avatar!

23:09.200 --> 23:10.450
I wear it now and then.

23:11.120 --> 23:14.450
Next, the Priest's Holy Robe, maxed out!

23:14.450 --> 23:17.330
When I remove this avatar,
my armor's on full display!

23:17.870 --> 23:21.540
Next, the Red Roses for the Queen Set!

23:21.540 --> 23:23.040
Looks so gorgeous!

23:23.040 --> 23:24.710
I don't really wear this that often!

23:25.300 --> 23:27.590
Last, but not least, my usual!

23:27.590 --> 23:29.840
So powerful, and it's my favorite!

23:30.300 --> 23:33.050
Thank you all for watching!

23:33.050 --> 23:38.180
Please look forward
to more hot tips from Rurihime!

23:38.180 --> 23:39.980
- Okay?
- Creepy!
